For Valks, who don't use spells so much, XL17 is enough to ascend [Well, I
guess someone will show me that for any class you can ascend a XL1
character]. If you don't need skill slots, then you don't need extra
levels. They will not necessarly be a harm [aparently, the frequencies of
Archon, eg, is much more dependant on the level of the sanctum than on
your own so being XL30 will not make the endgame significantly harder or
easier].

I think that you have enough HPs and stuffs, but more cannot harm. You
should, of course, top-enchant all your stuff and try to get more HPs via
alchemy or nurse dancing (that will makes your more confortable).
Bless-geno L and h (if you're no dwarf) can also help.

You may also want to switch for SDSM/cloak of MR in order to be able to
#twoweapon which can make things much easier in hell (especially if you
have a silver saber at hand).

But I don't think you *must* chase after levels. Well, you don't have to
run from wraith corpses, of course, but no need to run for them either. It
may evenbe better to leave wraith corpses/potions of GL to your pets [but
that is the best way to see a purple worm eat the said pet].

I've ascended twice (monk, both in nethack and slash'em) and almost
ascended once (valk, died on Fire) and I've never been more than XL17 (I
think, I'm sure no more than XL20).

